WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.538
A V P N address pool gives a
user an address on the network.

3
00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.827
If that user or device is compromised,

4
00:00:07.827 --> 00:00:12.849
the attacker can discover and move laterally
across everything the pool reaches.

5
00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:18.101
Private Access replaces the pool with
one path per application: its own hosts,

6
00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:22.285
ports and protocol, its own
assigned group, never individuals,

7
00:00:22.285 --> 00:00:25.813
and its own Conditional
Access, in report-only first.

8
00:00:25.813 --> 00:00:30.500
A compromised user or device can reach
what it was assigned, and nothing else.

9
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.387
Then the module does the same for
the paths an attacker wants most:

10
00:00:34.387 --> 00:00:38.995
administrative remote desktop, behind
phishing-resistant authentication,

11
00:00:38.995 --> 00:00:42.500
and domain controllers, behind
the Private Access sensor.
